+++ b/assets/guide.js
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@ window.NLBGuide = [
   {
     "group": "How-to guides",
     "title": "Invoices and payment plans",
-    "body": "<p>From a vendor dashboard, choose <b>Schedule payment</b> on a linked line, enter the payment amount and due date, and save. Repeat for separate dates; no automatic recurring payment is created. The simple flow splits base/fringes proportionally and cannot exceed the unscheduled balance. Use the existing advanced plan for shared payments, percentages, milestone dates or a custom split. Planning does not post to Actuals. Record paid explicitly; a shared payment is recorded once for all its allocations.</p><p><b>Add invoice…</b> records reference, type, recipient, issued/due dates, base/fringe amounts, note and supporting files. Duplicate references for the same recipient are rejected. Invoice information is entered manually; document reading is not implemented.</p><p>If an existing plan covers the same obligation, use <b>Link existing payment plan</b>. A blank invoice due date preserves a linked plan’s milestone timing. Do not enter the same bill as both an unrelated invoice and an extra plan.</p><p><b>Add payment plan…</b> creates an unpaid forecast: Fixed, Percentage or Remaining balance. Unpaid percentage/balance amounts follow applicable expected costs; posted paid amounts stay fixed. Shared fixed plans split their total across lines payable to one recipient. Base and fringes may be planned together or separately. Inapplicable controls are disabled with explanations.</p>"
+    "body": "<p><b>Schedule payment…</b> on a detail line starts the payment journey. Choose Expected or Confirmed and enter an expected date and, when known, a confirmed payment date. Leave the recipient TBD until known, then edit the same plan to assign it. For multiple payments, select the split option and add each separately. An unsplit amount updates the forecast, not the original budget or Actuals.</p><p>When due or overdue, a payment appears at the top of Payments. Choose Paid to review the final amount and explicitly post it. The final amount may differ from the forecast; uncheck the settle option for a partial payment. A recipient is required to record paid. Attach a receipt or explicitly skip it for now. Payments are not sent automatically.</p><p>From a vendor dashboard, choose <b>Schedule payment</b> on a linked line, enter the payment amount and due date, and save. Repeat for separate dates; no automatic recurring payment is created. The simple flow splits base/fringes proportionally and cannot exceed the unscheduled balance. Use the existing advanced plan for shared payments, percentages, milestone dates or a custom split. Planning does not post to Actuals. Record paid explicitly; a shared payment is recorded once for all its allocations.</p><p><b>Add invoice…</b> records reference, type, recipient, issued/due dates, base/fringe amounts, note and supporting files. Duplicate references for the same recipient are rejected. Invoice information is entered manually; document reading is not implemented.</p><p>If an existing plan covers the same obligation, use <b>Link existing payment plan</b>. A blank invoice due date preserves a linked plan’s milestone timing. Do not enter the same bill as both an unrelated invoice and an extra plan.</p><p><b>Add payment plan…</b> creates an unpaid forecast: Fixed, Percentage or Remaining balance. Unpaid percentage/balance amounts follow applicable expected costs; posted paid amounts stay fixed. Shared fixed plans split their total across lines payable to one recipient. Base and fringes may be planned together or separately. Inapplicable controls are disabled with explanations.</p>"
   },
   {
     "group": "How-to guides",
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@ window.NLBGuide = [
   {
     "group": "How-to guides",
     "title": "Production dates, funding and cash flow",
-    "body": "<p>Setup → Timeline &amp; Funding sets optional pre-production/production/post-production dates, custom milestones, opening cash and its as-of date. Use Edit timeline in the visual timeline to change production dates and opening cash. Select Custom milestone or Incoming funding beside Add milestone; both appear on the date axis. Expected and received funding have separate amounts/dates and an expectation does not record receipt.</p><p>Unpaid milestone-relative dates move when their milestone moves. Fixed dates and historical paid dates stay unchanged. Positive offsets mean days after; negative offsets mean days before. Cash Flow is budget-wide: it includes movements on/after the opening date, while earlier movements are already represented by opening cash. Expected funding is not money already in the bank.</p><p>Unallocated costs and undated installments remain <b>Not scheduled yet</b>. Contingency is a reserve, not invented dated spending. A reserve-funded allocation reduces remaining reserve without adding a second payment. Check missing dates and incoming funding before relying on a forecast.</p>"
+    "body": "<p>Setup → Timeline &amp; Funding sets optional pre-production/production/post-production dates, custom milestones, opening cash and its as-of date. Use Edit timeline in the visual timeline to change production dates and opening cash. Choose Add milestone, then Custom milestone or Incoming funding; both appear on the date axis. Expected and received funding have separate amounts/dates and an expectation does not record receipt.</p><p>Unpaid milestone-relative dates move when their milestone moves. Fixed dates and historical paid dates stay unchanged. Positive offsets mean days after; negative offsets mean days before. Cash Flow is budget-wide: it includes movements on/after the opening date, while earlier movements are already represented by opening cash. Expected funding is not money already in the bank.</p><p>Unallocated costs and undated installments remain <b>Not scheduled yet</b>. Contingency is a reserve, not invented dated spending. A reserve-funded allocation reduces remaining reserve without adding a second payment. Check missing dates and incoming funding before relying on a forecast.</p>"
   },
   {
     "group": "How-to guides",
diff --git a/assets/payments.css b/assets/payments.css
index 158a8c1..72391a7 100644
--- a/assets/payments.css
+++ b/assets/payments.css
@@ -121,3 +121,16 @@ input[type="date"],input[type="month"]{color-scheme:light}input[type="date"]::-w
 
 /* Dated payment markers in the budget-wide timeline. */
 .pt-scroll{max-height:620px;overflow:auto}.pt-account-group{margin:16px 0 4px;padding:7px 10px;background:var(--row-alt);border-radius:6px;font-weight:700;position:sticky;left:0;width:220px}.pt-line-row .pt-label small{font-size:11px}.pm-body .pt-payment-marker{position:absolute;z-index:2;transform:translateX(-50%);width:13px;height:13px;min-height:0;padding:0;border:1px solid var(--canvas);border-radius:50%}.pm-body .pt-payment-due{background:#e6a631}.pm-body .pt-payment-paid{background:#52b76e}.pm-body .pt-payment-marker:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--text);outline-offset:2px}.pm-cash-shortfall{border-color:#d7594e}.pt-overview .pt-scroll .pt-axis{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:5;background:var(--canvas)}
+/* Payment journey and focused timeline */
+.pm-backdrop,.pm-body,.pt-scroll{overscroll-behavior:contain}
+.pt-row>button{align-self:center;justify-self:center}
+.pt-add-menu{position:relative;display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;margin-left:8px}
+.pt-add-menu summary{list-style:none;cursor:pointer;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;padding:8px 10px;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;background:var(--accent);color:#171717}
+.pt-add-menu summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
+.pt-add-menu>div{position:absolute;right:0;z-index:5;min-width:170px;padding:6px;background:var(--canvas);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:7px;box-shadow:0 5px 18px #0003}
+.pt-add-menu>div button{display:block;width:100%;text-align:left;border:0}
+.lc-page-heading{justify-content:flex-start}.lc-page-heading>div{min-width:0}
+.journey-status{display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:16px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;margin:12px 0 20px}.journey-status legend{font-weight:600}.journey-status label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:5px}
+.journey-badge{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-weight:600}.journey-dot{display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;flex:none}.journey-red{background:#e25757}.journey-yellow{background:#e9ad2f}.journey-blue{background:#529fdd}.journey-green{background:#50b975}
+.journey-reminders{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:16px;margin-bottom:24px}.journey-reminders h3{margin:0}.journey-reminder{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}.journey-reminder small{display:block;color:var(--text-2);margin-top:4px}
+.journey-progress{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:16px;margin:14px 0}.journey-progress h4{margin:0 0 12px}.journey-progress ol{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0}.journey-progress li{flex:1;min-width:105px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:24px 1fr;column-gap:6px;align-items:center;color:var(--text-2)}.journey-progress li>span:first-child{grid-row:span 2;display:grid;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:50%}.journey-progress li.done{color:var(--text)}.journey-progress li.done>span:first-child{background:var(--accent);color:#171717;border-color:var(--accent)}.journey-progress li small{font-size:11px}
